{"id": "EUVD-2026-103905", "enisaUuid": "34390794-d818-3001-b5c7-1a11cf89f1d7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nblk-mq: set RQF_USE_SCHED when the operation is known\n\nThe cached requests are allocated for one operation but can be handed\nout for another. A passthrough command has RQF_USE_SCHED cleared, so\nusing those flags for a subsequent read/write bio will insert it into\nthe scheduler without ->prepare_request() and frees it without\n->finish_request(). For kyber, this leaks the domain token acquired at\ndispatch and stalls the queue.\n\nDon't set RQF_USE_SCHED based on the first operation the batch happened\nto be allocated for. Instead, set it after the request is claimed by an\noperation. Introduce a helper function, blk_mq_rq_late_init() for this,\nand absorb blk_mq_rq_time_init() since the two run together.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:49:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:26:13", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/790730e4d95de8356a573d4b4864486bba731863", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c47ebc27fa72078e26177cd458cdaf3006a9685", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab6c756f28c741d704a7c3e04814bfc3adf6f818"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98820", "GHSA-95f6-3pp2-9382"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04592733-b2b7-3640-afa6-6116ab4f9120", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b6a5d9cea911424e84107df8c4eb8317938d2cd <ab6c756f28c741d704a7c3e04814bfc3adf6f818"}, {"id": "0a503820-380e-3a03-aaf3-1a6675d3b1e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "10f64764-d522-37cf-948c-aef05ec302d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3eb9551d-e951-3b31-ba35-3a1a69744c58", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1"}, {"id": "6594872a-f03c-39dc-83f8-a329d7248758", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b6a5d9cea911424e84107df8c4eb8317938d2cd <2c47ebc27fa72078e26177cd458cdaf3006a9685"}, {"id": "7184c767-5d7d-3483-9236-8bb0fad44e77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4b6a5d9cea911424e84107df8c4eb8317938d2cd <790730e4d95de8356a573d4b4864486bba731863"}, {"id": "8f9f948b-5148-3fc9-988a-29714b1b2e1d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "ff4a5c39-ae7c-34fe-bf34-54630c7f4bc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f501278f-af82-3aa1-aba4-5d596ff1548e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}